hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1243","

Amr bin Khalid narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Maleeh narrated to us, saying: I heard Maimun bin Mihran saying: I asked Nafi: Was Ibn Umar used to invoke for the Moadibah? He said: But a donkey was once injured, so we slaughtered it. Then he said: Gather for me the people of Medina. Nafi said: So I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, for what purpose? We do not have bread. He said: O Allah, praise be to You. This is a raisin, and this is a grape, or he said: a grape and a quarter. Whoever wants to eat, and whoever wants to leave."," 'Did Ibn 'Umar ever\ninvite people to a banquet?' He said"," 'A camel of his once broke something\nand so we sacrificed it. Then Ibn 'Umar said"," \""Gather the people of Madina\nfor me.\"" I said"," \""Abu 'Abdu'r-Rahman"," for what? We do not have any bread.\""\nHe said"," \""O Allah"," praise belongs to You. These are bits of meat and this\nis broth","\"" or he said"," \""Broth and meat chunks. Whoever wishes can eat and\nwhoever wishes can leave it.\""'\"""""
"1244","Sa'ib ibn Yazid (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Some people from Quraysh would stand at the door of Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) — so that they might learn something — when the shadow began to decline"," he would say: 'Rise now"," for the time that remains is for the Shaytan.' Then he would pass by them and forcefully make them get up. While they were thus engaged"," it was said to them: 'This is a slave of Banu Hushaysh who recites poetry.' They called him and asked: 'What poetry did you recite?' He said: 'If you have resolved upon a morning journey"," then leave Salim"," for old age and the religion of Islam are sufficient to keep a person from evil.' He (Ibn Mas'ud) said: 'Enough"," you have spoken the truth"," you have spoken the truth.'\"""""
"1245","Sa'ib ibn Yazid (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates, he said: \Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would pass by us around midday and say: 'Rise and take a siqaylah (afternoon nap)"," for the time that remains is for the Shaytan.'\"""""
"1246","Sayyiduna Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that he would perform the Friday prayer and then take a siqaylah (afternoon nap)."
"1247","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: \When the prohibition of wine was revealed"," the preferred wine of the people of Madinah was made from dried dates and fresh dates. One day"," I was serving wine to the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at the house of Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him)"," when a man passed by and said: 'Wine has been made unlawful.' He (Abu Talhah) did not ask when it had become unlawful or investigate the matter; rather he said: 'O Anas"," pour this wine away.' Then he took a siqaylah (afternoon nap) at the house of Umm Sulaym until the intensity of the sun diminished"," and he performed ghusl (ritual bath). Then Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) applied perfume to him. Then he came into the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and the situation was just as the man had described. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: 'After that"," he never again put wine to his lips.'\"""""
"1248","Khawwat ibn Jubayr (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates, he said: \Sleep during the first part of the day is ignorance"," sleeping during the middle part is a good habit"," and sleeping during the latter part is foolishness.\"""""
